HikisTrack modifications (September 2026)

The earlier Live Inputs change list above documents the supplied base. This
distribution replaces its local-only replay-finish behavior with normal completed-
run submissions, and exports Miso2 without fork-only map/account lock flags.

Additional work: native desktop worker bridge; binary physics result transport;
practice prefix restoration; unified clip library and keybinds; release threshold;
ghost tools; PT Index integration; Electron packaging for Windows and macOS.

PolySim by SpideyZac: https://github.com/SpideyZac/polysim
Its license is included in native/polysim/LICENSE in the source archive.
The PolySim source and BruteForce runner incorporate the user's existing
August 2026 local native-engine work, with additional desktop worker support.

PT Index uses the user's supplied September 2026 source: ranking.ts,
kacky-ranking.ts, identity.ts, map lists and snapshots are retained in index-source
and index-data. Electron and its bundled third-party license notices accompany
the packaged runtime. PolyTrack game and asset attribution is retained.

Version 1.1 incorporates the editor, main/preload IPC bridge, BruteForce modules,
renderer trigger/geometry helpers and bundled dependencies from the user's
September 5, 2026 BruteForce app.asar. Original clip-row styles are reused with
map folders and search. Replay application, speed/submit controls and persistent
input-overlay attachment are integrated with the Rust desktop simulation bridge.
